  "decision_conditions": [
    "The Tree Works that are carried shall not exceed the description of the Tree Works amounts as described in Section 7 of the Application Form that was submitted to the Council. \r\rReason: To ensure the preservation of the amenity value and health of the tree(s).\r",
    "This decision notice for Tree Works is only valid for 2 years from the date of this decision or until the work is completed, whichever is the sooner. \r\rReason: In order to ensure that the work is carried out whilst still appropriate and in accordance with the time period within the legislation and regulations.",
    "A replacement tree for the Horse Chestnut shall be planted in accordance with the following specifications:\r\rTree Species: Wild Service Tree (Sorbus torminalis) or Sweet Gum (Liquidambar styraciflua).\rQuantity: x1.\rSize/Height: 14-16cm stem circumference at 1m, to be planted in accordance with the recommendations in British Standard 8545: Trees from nursery to independence in the landscape - Recommendations (2014). Root ball or container grown is acceptable.\rLocation: Within 4 metres of felled tree, or in an alternative position to be agreed in writing by the Council.\rDeadline: Within 6 months following the removal of the original tree to coincide with the planting season, or an alternative date to be agreed in writing by the Council.\r\rThe tree shall thereafter be maintained and shall not be pruned or removed without the written consent of the Council."
  ],
